bpfcc (0.31.0+ds-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  Starting with this version, all binary files for the libbpf-tools
  package have been renamed to $filename-libbpf suffix.
  .
  For example: execsnoop => execsnoop-libbpf
  .
  This is to ensure that we have consistency across the different
  variants of the tools, namely: bpfcc-tools, perf-tools-unstable and
  libbpf-tools

 -- Ritesh Raj Sarraf <rrs@debian.org>  Mon, 17 Mar 2025 15:06:03 +0530

bpfcc (0.2.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  Starting with version 0.2.0-2, all binary files have been renamed to
  $filename-bpfcc suffix.
  .
  For example: execsnoop => execsnoop-bpfcc
  .
  Similarly, the manpages have been renamed. This is done to accommodate
  users who would like to use perf-tools-unstable, parallelly with the
  eBPF Compiler Collection Tools from the bpfcc package.
  .
  Both upstreams work closely on the projects, thus the common names.

 -- Ritesh Raj Sarraf <rrs@debian.org>  Fri, 30 Dec 2016 23:42:55 +0530
